One ChatGPT Link Could Be Dangerous
Security researchers found a new risk.
A person may receive a ChatGPT link from someone else.
The link can hide instructions for an AI agent.
If the AI agent follows these hidden instructions, it may do things the user did not expect.
In a company, this could be a serious problem.
The AI agent might read private information or perform unwanted actions.
Researchers say companies should be careful when using AI agents.
People should not trust every link they receive.
Developers also need better security to stop hidden instructions from controlling AI systems.
The writer says AI agents can save time, but they also create new security risks.
Everyone should use them carefully.
